WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.268
-You know what I wanted to
bring up to you?

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.870
Because it was on the TV
the other day,

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.838
and I couldn't turn it off,
because you're amazing in it --

00:00:05.838 --> 00:00:07.573
but it was "Lincoln."
-Yeah.

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:10.109
-Steven Spielberg's movie
about Abraham Lincoln.

00:00:10.109 --> 00:00:11.844
-That was so much fun.

00:00:11.844 --> 00:00:13.146
-You were amazing in that one.

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:14.380
I mean, you're always great,

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.115
but this,
you were in the zone, dude.

00:00:16.115 --> 00:00:17.817
It was great.
-It was so much fun.

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:20.352
-Did you learn anything?
Or what was Steven like?

00:00:20.352 --> 00:00:22.322
Like, was he -- Did you --

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:25.725
-I'd known him beforehand
just socially,

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:27.960
but I had never worked
with him before.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.797
And he was -- he's just
absolutely lovely to work with.

00:00:31.797 --> 00:00:33.065
I remember I showed up one day,

00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:34.601
and I was walking along
with him,

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.536
and it was the beginning of the
day, and we had a big sequence.

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:38.571
There was --
in front of the Capitol,

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:42.375
and it was a -- all these horses
and carriages,

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.043
I mean, dozens and dozens
of them,

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:47.313
and on this big, huge set that
had turned it into a dirt road

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:52.084
and, you know, extras all over
the place and military

00:00:52.084 --> 00:00:53.552
and all the rest of that.

00:00:53.552 --> 00:00:55.255
And I went up, I said, "Steven,
what do you --

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:57.857
what do you think for this?"

00:00:57.857 --> 00:01:00.894
And he said -- He looked around
at everything that was going on

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:03.495
and he said, "I don't know.

00:01:03.495 --> 00:01:04.497
We'll figure it out."

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:05.565
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:08.368
And that sort of
level of confidence,

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:11.303
what it breeds
is tremendous creativity,

00:01:11.303 --> 00:01:14.840
because you are able
to discover things.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.543
-And you're trusting everyone
that's working with you.

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:20.713
-Yeah, and he has great trust
in the people he works with.

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:23.682
He's -- I find him
lovely to work with.

00:01:23.682 --> 00:01:25.885
And the film
was just so wonderful.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:28.955
-And every every single cutaway
to you and every reaction,

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:30.423
I was like,
"That's how you do it."

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:33.092
If you want to watch
good acting, watch James Spader.

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:35.929
James, thank you so much
for being on our show.

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:37.663
"The Blacklist," everybody.

00:01:37.663 --> 00:01:40.366
Let's take a look at a clip
from next Friday's episode.

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:41.634
Take a look.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.603
-Your message said you wanted
to talk to Priya.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:45.171
She's my most valuable asset.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:48.107
-Which is why I want her
to be an asset of mine.

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:52.245
If she agrees, I'll compensate
you for your loss.

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:53.713
-Pennies on the dollar.

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:55.781
-Pennies on the dollar?!

00:01:55.781 --> 00:01:57.550
Dembe, are you listening
to this?

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:02.288
Penny -- I've never paid pennies
on the dollar in my life.

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:05.658
If I'm known for anything,
it's for overpaying.

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:09.495
He's forever trying to get me
to show some restraint.

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:11.531
But listen, we can
resolve this right now.

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:14.400
I can get Edward to take it up
to a few thousand feet,

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.537
circle back around,
come in over the 18th hole,

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:20.272
and drop you
right into the grandstand.

00:02:20.272 --> 00:02:23.375
We've done it before.
I'm sure we'll do it again.

00:02:23.375 --> 00:02:26.078
-Yeah, that's exactly right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:26.078 --> 00:02:28.781
Come on!
James Spader, everybody!

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:32.585
Catch "The Blacklist" Fridays
at 8:00 p.m. on NBC.

